<speak>Thank you. I'll bring up my prepared notes now. So your objective is long-term wealth growth through diversified global equity exposure, rather than funding immediate spending, and you prefer a straightforward holding without frequent monitoring. With Summit Global Equity <sub alias="ee tee eff">ETF</sub>, a broad decline in global share markets can pull down the value of its underlying holdings and the fund itself. Diversification may not protect you when markets fall together. Do you understand that the fund can fall in value during a global market decline, even though its holdings are diversified?</speak>